  "method": [
    "Disposable local catalog and protected app data. Only dummy key input is supplied through actual native secure fields. Never read personal credentials.",
    "Actual production renderer/preload and bundled main/service/storage. The shared-key adapter returns null/no-op. All nonlocal provider requests and server writes are blocked; scheduler is stopped. Initial ready-to-show is suppressed only in the fixture, then the owned window is shown at the accepted baseline.",
    "A snapshotHold gate executes a real status read after sender/input guards, then holds its old result. Native explicit Save commits each of three provider keys. Release original empty statuses only after all three Key saved states; none regresses.",
    "Native explicit Remove starts all three held setters. General/Provider keys navigation mounts actual reads while removal remains pending; those reads retain old configured results. Release only setters, verify all No key configured states, then release obsolete configured reads and verify they cannot restore Remove actions.",
    "For OpenAI, hold a save and start an old empty read during it. Release setter through a controlled commitFail gate: actual local save commits before modeled lost confirmation. The failure callback cancels the old query and reads current saved status, with entered draft/error/editability retained. Releasing the old result cannot replace the fresh status.",
    "Native CUA supplies all Settings navigation, secure-field typing and Save/Remove. Playwright is launch/read-only observation; command files change only named fixture timing/fault gates. No key text, keypress stream, protected files or input lengths are included in this committed record."
